<title>VIETNAM: Indonesia coffee output seen steady, exports up.</title>
<headline>Indonesia coffee output seen steady, exports up.</headline>
<dateline>HO CHI MINH CITY, Vietnam 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian coffee production in 1997 is seen remaining steady at about 480,000 tonnes, while exports will rise slightly to 350,000 tonnes from 344,000, an official of the Association of Indonesian Coffee Exporters said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Litha Brent told Reuters in an interview at an Asia coffee conference here that domestic coffee consumption would probably remain steady at more than 100,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>&quot;The production and export situation should remain the same with exports going up only slightly,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Indonesia is the biggest coffee producer in Asia and ranks third in the world behind Brazil and Colombia.</p>
</text>
